<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Seon of Balhae</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. <a href="/years/818">818</a>–830</span> · <a href="/centuries/9th-century">9th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zen">Seon</a> was the tenth king of Balhae, ruling from 818 to 830. He subdued neighbouring <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mohe">Mohe</a> tribes and expanded the kingdom to its greatest extent in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manchuria">Manchuria</a> and northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/korea">Korea</a>, and its organisation into five capitals and fifteen prefectures is associated with his reign. Chinese sources came to call Balhae the 'flourishing land in the east'.</p></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>Under King <b>Seon</b> (r. 818–830) campaigns against the Mohe tribes of the north extended Balhae rule towards the Amur and Ussuri rivers.</blockquote><a href="/empire/balhae">Balhae · Military</a></li><li><blockquote>It disappears from the records in the early 9th century and is usually thought to have been absorbed by Balhae under King <b>Seon</b> around 820.</blockquote><a href="/state/lesser-goguryeo">Lesser Goguryeo</a></li></ul></section>
